# Build context exclusions for the production image (see Dockerfile).
#
# Three things MUST stay in the context or the build breaks in non-obvious
# ways, so do not add them here:
#   * pnpm-workspace.yaml — carries onlyBuiltDependencies; without it pnpm 10
#     blocks the bcrypt and @prisma/engines postinstall scripts.
#   * prisma/ — schema.prisma drives `prisma generate`, migrations/ ships so
#     `prisma migrate deploy` can be exec'd against the running container.
#   * scripts/ — verify_google_purchase.py + requirements.txt are resolved at
#     runtime from process.cwd().

# Dependencies and build output — rebuilt inside the image, and a host-built
# node_modules would be the wrong architecture (amd64 dev box -> arm64 image).
node_modules
**/node_modules
dist
build
.pnpm-store

# Secrets. Nothing environment-specific belongs in a layer; config comes from
# SSM at runtime.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*.p8
*.p12
gcp-*.json
service-account*.json

# VCS / CI / editor
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.githooks
.github
.gitlab-ci.yml
.vscode
.idea
.devcontainer
.claude
.superpowers
*.swp
.DS_Store

# Tests, fixtures and coverage — not shipped and not needed to build.
test
coverage
.nyc_output
**/*.spec.ts
**/*.e2e-spec.ts
__mocks__
jest.config.js
postman_full_collection.json

# Puppeteer / mermaid-cli junk. @mermaid-js/mermaid-cli is a devDependency
# used only for generating diagrams; its Chromium cache and rendered output
# must never enter the context.
.cache
.local-chromium
puppeteer-cache
.puppeteerrc*
**/*.mmd
mermaid.config.json

# Local dev orchestration and the PM2 deployment path this image replaces.
docker-compose*.yml
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
ecosystem.config.js
deploy
monitoring

# Docs and logs
*.md
!README.md
docs
logs
*.log
tmp
uploads
